---
import { site } from '../../config/site';

/** Legal notice in English. Courtesy translation of `LegalFr.astro` (the French text prevails): keep both aligned. */
const { legal } = site;
const todo = 'to be completed';
const status = legal.status === 'entrepreneur individuel' ? 'sole trader (entrepreneur individuel)' : legal.status;
const updated = 'October 15, 2026';
---

<h1 class="text-3xl font-medium">Legal notice</h1>
<p>In accordance with French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004 on confidence in the digital economy (LCEN) and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Last updated: {updated}.</p>
<p>This English version is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the French version prevails.</p>

<h2>Site publisher</h2>
<p>
  <strong>{site.name}</strong>, {status ?? todo}, working as a freelance web developer.<br />
  SIRET: {legal.siret ?? todo}<br />
  Address: {legal.address ?? todo}<br />
  {legal.vat ? <>EU VAT number: {legal.vat}<br /></> : legal.vatFranchise ? <>VAT not applicable, article 293 B of the French General Tax Code<br /></> : null}
  Email: <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
</p>
<p><strong>Publication director:</strong> {site.name}.</p>

<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>
  Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, United States ·
  <a class="underline" href="https://www.cloudflare.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cloudflare.com<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a>.
</p>

<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
<p>
  The texts, layout, graphic design and code of this site are the property of {site.name}, unless stated otherwise.
  The source code is published under the MIT licence on <a class="underline" href={site.links.github} rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a>;
  the licence does not cover the texts, images, or the brands and logos shown.
</p>
<p>
  The names, logos and screenshots of the clients and projects mentioned (French National Gendarmerie, Trik3r Collecte and others) belong to their
  respective owners and are shown as professional references. For any removal or correction request,
  write to the address above.
</p>

<h2 id="donnees">Personal data</h2>
<h3>Data controller</h3>
<p>{site.name}, at the contact details given above.</p>

<h3>Contact form</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Data:</strong> name, email address, company and budget (optional), project type and message content.</li>
  <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> answering your request and, where applicable, preparing a quote.</li>
  <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> pre-contractual measures taken at your request, then legitimate interest in following up the relationship (art. 6.1 b and f of the GDPR).</li>
  <li><strong>Retention period:</strong> for the duration of the exchange, then at most 3 years after the last contact if no contract is concluded; if a contract is concluded, for the legal retention period of commercial and accounting records.</li>
  <li><strong>Recipients:</strong> {site.name} only. No data is sold or transferred for commercial purposes.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Processors and transfers outside the European Union</h3>
<p>
  The message passes through technical service providers: Cloudflare (hosting and execution of the form), Resend (sending of emails) and
  {site.name}'s email provider. These providers may process data in the United States; transfers are covered by
  the European Commission's standard contractual clauses or by the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
  The form does not store any request in a database of its own.
</p>

<h3>Your rights</h3>
<p>
  You have the right to access, rectify, erase, object to, restrict and port your data.
  To exercise them, write to <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>; you will receive an answer
  within one month. If you disagree, you may lodge a complaint with the
  <a class="underline" href="https://www.cnil.fr/fr/plaintes" rel="noopener" target="_blank">CNIL (French data protection authority)<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a>.
</p>

<h2>Cookies and audience measurement</h2>
<p>
  This site does not set any cookie or tracker requiring your consent. Traffic is measured with Umami, a cookie-free tool
  that does not collect any personal data and does not allow a visitor to be tracked from one site to another; your data is not
  cross-referenced with other sources. Fonts are hosted on the site itself: no request is sent to a third-party font service.
  Your choice of light or dark theme is remembered in your browser (local storage), only for your display comfort. The site language is
  determined by the address of the page you visit and is not stored.
</p>

<h2>External links</h2>
<p>
  This site links to third-party sites (projects, professional profiles). {site.name} has no control over their content and
  accepts no responsibility for their practices.
</p>

<h2 id="accessibilite">Accessibility</h2>
<p>
  {site.name} is committed to making this site accessible, in accordance with article 47 of French law no. 2005-102 of 11 February 2005, aiming for level AA
  of the French accessibility guidelines (RGAA) and of WCAG 2.2.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Conformance status:</strong> not formally assessed. No full RGAA audit has been carried out. Automated checks
  (axe-core, on all pages, in light and dark themes) report no issue and the site can be navigated with a keyboard, but these checks
  only cover part of the criteria: the site is therefore not declared compliant.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Measures in place:</strong> light or dark theme of your choice, high colour contrast, skip link, keyboard navigation,
  respect for your system's "reduce motion" setting, and a button to pause the home page headline animation.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Reporting a problem:</strong> if you cannot access some content, write to
  <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>; you will receive an answer within 10 working days, with an
  accessible alternative if needed. If it does not satisfy you, you can refer the matter to the
  <a class="underline" href="https://formulaire.defenseurdesdroits.fr" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Défenseur des droits (French Rights Defender)<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a>.
</p>

<h2>Liability</h2>
<p>
  The content of the site is provided for information purposes and may be modified at any time. {site.name} endeavours to ensure its
  accuracy but cannot be held liable for any error, omission or temporary unavailability of the site.
</p>

<h2>Terms of sale and mediation</h2>
<p>
  Services are not sold online: each assignment is covered by a written quote specifying the scope, price, deadlines
  and payment terms, which are binding between the parties.
</p>
<p>
  For a client acting as a consumer, any dispute may be submitted free of charge to a consumer mediator:
  {legal.mediator ?? todo}.
</p>

<h2>Applicable law</h2>
<p>This site and its terms of use are governed by French law. Any dispute falls within the jurisdiction of the competent courts.</p>
